Original commit body from 73739c189cb2c38074b2769c81f13cbc9f5951f9:

FileIndex.match_pattern fnmatched every glob against the bare file
name, which never holds a '/', so under the index every survey installs
a pattern with a directory segment matched nothing. Lost in production,
found in unit tests (which run without an index):
- requirements.py 'requirements/*.txt', 'reqs/*.txt'
- play_routes.py 'conf/*.routes' partials and '*/conf/routes'
- di_resolution 'META-INF/services/*' (Maven-layout ServiceLoader
  bindings under src/main/resources)
- sketch TEST_FILE_PATTERNS '__tests__/*.js', '__tests__/*.ts'

match_pattern now matches such a pattern against the path relative to
the requested root (find_files passes it), segment by segment with
'**' spanning any number, anchored at the end: rglob's rule.

The new guard compares both find_files paths on every literal pattern
the source tree declares (file_patterns, pattern lists, find_files /
find_non_test_files call literals: 297 of 430 collected, placed at two
depths). It found two more divergences of the same invariant, both
fixed toward the index (production) behaviour:
- pure '*.ext' patterns: the index matched Path.suffix
  case-insensitively, rglob case-sensitively ('*.h' vs Foo.H). One
  helper, _pure_extension, now drives both paths.
- a file two patterns match ('*.R' and '*.r'; '*.py' and 'test_*.py')
  was yielded once by the index and twice by the walk; the walk now
  dedups too.

Live check (scratch tree): walk and index now agree on
META-INF/services/*, __tests__/*.js, conf/*.routes and *.h (Foo.H).
smart-test affected set before the dedup: 20775 passed, 14 failed
(all R/Fortran duplicate-file tests, fixed by the dedup); those 14
plus the new tests: 179 passed.

